          "preset": "max_width_1440",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Nov 17 2022 01:32:06 GMT+0000",
          "alt": "System offerings",
          "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/trauma-and-extremeties/products/variaxwristfusion/images/Family.png",
          "borderColor": "rgba(76,125,122,1)",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Dec 15 2022 00:04:23 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
          "enableBorder": "false"
        }
      },
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_copy_copy_47067": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-5891a4f69d@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Mon Aug 22 2022 22:16:19 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Although wrist fusion is a relatively rare indication, it may be an effective treatment for chronic wrist joint pain. The VariAx 2 Wrist Fusion System is a range of titanium plates which are contoured to bridge the radius and metacarpal bones to allow for stable fixation during fusion osteosynthesis. The plating system uses the VariAx 2 screws and instrumentation platform which includes variable-angled locking and non-locking screws. Made of titanium and treated with a Type II anodization, these plates are designed to carry the loads that are required of them while remaining low profile.</span></span><br>\n</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Nov 21 2022 04:24:35 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
    "cols2_1_3_2_3_114006": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Nov 17 2022 01:31:59 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Nov 17 2022 01:31:59 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_1-3_2-3",
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "standaloneimage": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-b2cf110515@example.invalid",
          "preset": "max_width_auto",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Nov 17 2022 01:32:06 GMT+0000",
          "alt": "Plate options",
          "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/trauma-and-extremeties/products/variaxwristfusion/images/Family-side.jpg",
          "borderColor": "rgba(76,125,122,1)",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Jan 13 2023 16:15:23 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
          "enableBorder": "false"
        }
      },
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_copy_copy_47067": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-5891a4f69d@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Mon Aug 22 2022 22:16:19 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">The VariAx 2 Wrist Fusion System offers 3 types of plates from which to choose: Standard Bend Plate, Short Bend Plate, and Straight Plate.&nbsp; The bended plates contain 4 proximal holes for distal radius fixation and 4 distal holes for metacarpal fixation. Within the bend of the plate, there is an additional hole for capitate fixation.&nbsp; The straight plate is also designed with 4 proximal and distal holes; however, there are 2 additional holes located centrally for carpal fixation.&nbsp; Plate Trials may be provided to determine the proper plate to be implanted. This may be particularly useful when using sterile-packed plates.</span></span><br>\n</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Nov 21 2022 04:24:45 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
    "cols2_1_3_2_3_114006_1808004795": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Nov 17 2022 01:31:59 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Nov 17 2022 01:31:59 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_1-3_2-3",
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "standaloneimage": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
          "preset": "max_width_1440",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Nov 17 2022 01:32:06 GMT+0000",
          "alt": "screw options",
          "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/trauma-and-extremeties/products/variaxwristfusion/images/Screws.png",
          "borderColor": "rgba(76,125,122,1)",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Dec 15 2022 00:04:48 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
          "enableBorder": "false"
        }
      },
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_copy_copy_47067": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-5891a4f69d@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-b2cf110515@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Mon Aug 22 2022 22:16:19 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">For all plates, the distal radius holes are to be filled with 3.5mm (Orange). For the carpal and metacarpal holes, 2.7mm (Purple) or 2.4mm (Blue) screws are to be used.&nbsp; The circular holes in the plates provide an option for locking and non–locking. In order to distinguish a locking screw from a non-locking screw, the top of the locking screw heads are laser marked with a black circular ring and inner dot.</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">The polyaxial locking technology works by using two different grades of titanium. Locking screws are made of titanium alloy (Ti6Al4V) and when a screw is driven into a plate hole, the locking threads on the underside of the screw head engage the circular ‘lip’ in the hole.&nbsp; This technology allows the surgeon to aim and lock the screw within a 30° cone.</span></span><br>\n</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Jan 12 2023 21:44:29 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
